IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg10-sos-service`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, Subchapter XVI (ss 371-380): FOREIGN CORPORATIONS -- who is a
-- foreign corporation, how it qualifies to do business in this State, what it files when it changes, which
-- corporations are excused, the annual report, service of process on a qualified foreign corporation, the change
-- of registered agent and reinstatement, fines, banking powers and acting as a fiduciary.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone (src:1829-1906).
-- (ss 381-385 are in dg10-foreign-withdrawal-and-suits.l4.)
--
-- Quote lines are slices of de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text): `-- src:N | ...` is line N.
--
-- Subchapter XVI is outside the stockholder-to-member reading of s 114(a) for a nonstock corporation (s 114(b)(3)).
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation, read for this subchapter as a
-- director, officer, incorporator or stockholder of the foreign corporation concerned (a foreign corporation is not
-- a Delaware corporation, so the brief's seat is applied to the corporation these sections are about), or the
-- agent of such a corporation.

§ `Subchapter XVI. Foreign Corporations`

§§ `s 371 Definition; qualification to do business in State; procedure`

-- src:1832 | (a) As used in this chapter, the words “foreign corporation” mean a corporation organized under the laws of any jurisdiction other than this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(a) (src:1832)
GIVEN `where the corporation was organized` IS A `Where an entity is formed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(a) the corporation is a foreign corporation` `where the corporation was organized` MEANS
    NOT (`where the corporation was organized` EQUALS `this State`)

-- (b)(1): "A certificate, as of a date not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date, issued by an authorized
-- officer of the jurisdiction of its incorporation evidencing its corporate existence. If such certificate is in a
-- foreign language, a translation thereof, under oath of the translator, shall be attached thereto". Six months
-- before the filing date is counted with the core's month arithmetic (31 August less 6 months is 28 February);
-- the day six months before is inside the period (fork F28).
-- src:1834 | (1) A certificate, as of a date not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date, issued by an authorized officer of the jurisdiction of its incorporation evidencing its corporate existence. If such certificate is in a foreign language, a translation thereof, under oath of the translator, shall be attached thereto;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b)(1) (src:1834)
DECLARE `s 371(b)(1) Certificate of corporate existence` HAS
    `the date of the certificate`                                                                                    IS A DATE
    `the certificate was issued by an authorized officer of the jurisdiction of incorporation`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate evidences the foreign corporation's corporate existence`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate is in a foreign language`                                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a translation of the certificate, under oath of the translator, is attached`                                   IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1834 | (1) A certificate, as of a date not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date, issued by an authorized officer of the jurisdiction of its incorporation evidencing its corporate existence. If such certificate is in a foreign language, a translation thereof, under oath of the translator, shall be attached thereto;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b)(1) (src:1834)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 371(b)(1) Certificate of corporate existence`
      `the filing date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(b)(1) the certificate meets the paragraph` certificate `the filing date` MEANS
        certificate's `the date of the certificate` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in months` 6) `before` `the filing date`)
    AND certificate's `the certificate was issued by an authorized officer of the jurisdiction of incorporation`
    AND certificate's `the certificate evidences the foreign corporation's corporate existence`
    AND ((NOT certificate's `the certificate is in a foreign language`) OR certificate's `a translation of the certificate, under oath of the translator, is attached`)

-- (b)(2)(i): the registered agent "may be any of the foreign corporation itself, an individual resident in this State, a
-- domestic corporation, a domestic partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or
-- limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic limited liability company, a domestic
-- statutory trust, a foreign corporation (other than the foreign corporation itself), a foreign partnership ..., a
-- foreign limited liability company or a foreign statutory trust." The list is read as closed (fork F24).
-- src:1835 | which agent may be any of the foreign corporation itself, an individual resident in this State, a domestic corporation, a domestic partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic limited liability company, a domestic statutory trust, a foreign corporation (other than the foreign corporation itself), a foreign partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a foreign limited liability company or a foreign statutory trust, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b)(2) (src:1835)
GIVEN `the registered agent is the foreign corporation itself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the kind of the registered agent` IS A `Kind of entity`
      `the registered agent is an individual resident in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(b)(2)(i) the registered agent is one that the subparagraph allows` `the registered agent is the foreign corporation itself` `the kind of the registered agent` `the registered agent is an individual resident in this State` MEANS
    IF `the registered agent is the foreign corporation itself`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the kind of the registered agent`
          WHEN `a natural person` THEN `the registered agent is an individual resident in this State`
          WHEN `a corporation` k THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a general partnership` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a limited partnership` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a limited liability company` THEN TRUE
          WHEN `a statutory trust` THEN TRUE
          OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- src:1835 | (2) A statement executed by an authorized officer of each corporation setting forth (i) the name and address of its registered agent in this State, which agent may be any of the foreign corporation itself, an individual resident in this State, a domestic corporation, a domestic partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic limited liability company, a domestic statutory trust, a foreign corporation (other than the foreign corporation itself), a foreign partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a foreign limited liability company or a foreign statutory trust, (ii) a statement, as of a date not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date, of the assets and liabilities of the corporation, and (iii) the business it proposes to do in this State, and a statement that it is authorized to do that business in the jurisdiction of its incorporation. The statement shall be acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b)(2) (src:1835)
DECLARE `s 371(b)(2) Statement of the foreign corporation` HAS
    `the statement was executed by an authorized officer of the corporation`                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement sets forth the name and address of its registered agent in this State`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the registered agent is one that s 371(b)(2)(i) allows`                                                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date as of which the statement of the assets and liabilities of the corporation is made`                                      IS A DATE
    `the statement sets forth the assets and liabilities of the corporation`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement sets forth the business the corporation proposes to do in this State and that it is authorized to do that business in the jurisdiction of its incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the statement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103`                                                                           IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)

-- src:1835 | (2) A statement executed by an authorized officer of each corporation setting forth (i) the name and address of its registered agent in this State, which agent may be any of the foreign corporation itself, an individual resident in this State, a domestic corporation, a domestic partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a domestic limited liability company, a domestic statutory trust, a foreign corporation (other than the foreign corporation itself), a foreign partnership (whether general (including a limited liability partnership) or limited (including a limited liability limited partnership)), a foreign limited liability company or a foreign statutory trust, (ii) a statement, as of a date not earlier than 6 months prior to the filing date, of the assets and liabilities of the corporation, and (iii) the business it proposes to do in this State, and a statement that it is authorized to do that business in the jurisdiction of its incorporation. The statement shall be acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b)(2) (src:1835)
GIVEN statement IS A `s 371(b)(2) Statement of the foreign corporation`
      `the filing date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(b)(2) the statement meets the paragraph` statement `the filing date` MEANS
        statement's `the statement was executed by an authorized officer of the corporation`
    AND statement's `the statement sets forth the name and address of its registered agent in this State`
    AND statement's `the registered agent is one that s 371(b)(2)(i) allows`
    AND statement's `the date as of which the statement of the assets and liabilities of the corporation is made` AT LEAST (`the date` (`period in months` 6) `before` `the filing date`)
    AND statement's `the statement sets forth the assets and liabilities of the corporation`
    AND statement's `the statement sets forth the business the corporation proposes to do in this State and that it is authorized to do that business in the jurisdiction of its incorporation`
    AND statement's `the statement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103`

-- (b): "until it shall have paid to the Secretary of State of this State for the use of this State, $80, and shall have
-- filed ... (1) ... (2) ..."
-- src:1833 | (b) No foreign corporation shall do any business in this State, through or by branch offices, agents or representatives located in this State, until it shall have paid to the Secretary of State of this State for the use of this State, $80, and shall have filed in the office of the Secretary of State:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b) (src:1833)
GIVEN `the amount the foreign corporation paid the Secretary of State for the use of this State` IS A NUMBER
      certificate IS A `s 371(b)(1) Certificate of corporate existence`
      statement IS A `s 371(b)(2) Statement of the foreign corporation`
      `the filing date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(b) the foreign corporation has paid and filed what the subsection requires` `the amount the foreign corporation paid the Secretary of State for the use of this State` certificate statement `the filing date` MEANS
        `the amount the foreign corporation paid the Secretary of State for the use of this State` AT LEAST 80
    AND `s 371(b)(1) the certificate meets the paragraph` certificate `the filing date`
    AND `s 371(b)(2) the statement meets the paragraph` statement `the filing date`

-- "No foreign corporation shall do any business in this State, through or by branch offices, agents or
-- representatives located in this State, until it shall have paid ... and shall have filed": it may do business when
-- it has qualified, or when s 373 excuses it from ss 371 and 372.
-- src:1833 | No foreign corporation shall do any business in this State, through or by branch offices, agents or representatives located in this State, until it shall have paid to the Secretary of State of this State for the use of this State, $80, and shall have filed in the office of the Secretary of State:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(b) (src:1833)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation has paid and filed what s 371(b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporation is excused from ss 371 and 372 by s 373(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(b) the foreign corporation may do business in this State through branch offices, agents or representatives located here` `the foreign corporation has paid and filed what s 371(b) requires` `the foreign corporation is excused from ss 371 and 372 by s 373(a)` MEANS
    `the foreign corporation has paid and filed what s 371(b) requires` OR `the foreign corporation is excused from ss 371 and 372 by s 373(a)`

-- (c): the Secretary of State's certificate, delivered to the registered agent on payment of the fee, "shall be prima
-- facie evidence of the right of the corporation to do business in this State".
-- src:1836 | The certificate of the Secretary of State, under seal of office, of the filing of the certificates required by subsection (b) of this section, shall be delivered to the registered agent upon the payment to the Secretary of State of the fee prescribed for such certificates, and the certificate shall be prima facie evidence of the right of the corporation to do business in this State; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(c) (src:1836)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has delivered the certificate of the filing to the registered agent upon payment of the fee prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 391 (piece dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(c) the certificate of the Secretary of State is prima facie evidence of the right to do business in this State` `the Secretary of State has delivered the certificate of the filing to the registered agent upon payment of the fee prescribed` MEANS
    `the Secretary of State has delivered the certificate of the filing to the registered agent upon payment of the fee prescribed`

-- "the Secretary of State shall not issue such certificate unless the name of the corporation is such as to
-- distinguish it upon the records in the office of the Division of Corporations ... from the names that are reserved
-- ... and from the names ... of each other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company
-- or statutory trust ..., except with the written consent of the person who has reserved such name or such other
-- corporation, partnership, ... executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with s 103."
-- src:1836 | provided, that the Secretary of State shall not issue such certificate unless the name of the corporation is such as to distinguish it upon the records in the office of the Division of Corporations in the Department of State from the names that are reserved on such records and from the names on such records of each other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust organized or registered as a domestic or foreign corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust under the laws of this State, except with the written consent of the person who has reserved such name or such other corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust, executed, acknowledged and filed with the Secretary of State in accordance with § 103 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(c) (src:1836)
GIVEN `the name distinguishes the corporation upon the records of the Division of Corporations from the reserved names and from the names of the other entities organized or registered as domestic or foreign entities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who reserved the name or the other entity has consented in writing, executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(c) the Secretary of State may issue the certificate as to the name` `the name distinguishes the corporation upon the records of the Division of Corporations from the reserved names and from the names of the other entities organized or registered as domestic or foreign entities` `the person who reserved the name or the other entity has consented in writing, executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103` MEANS
        `the name distinguishes the corporation upon the records of the Division of Corporations from the reserved names and from the names of the other entities organized or registered as domestic or foreign entities`
    OR  `the person who reserved the name or the other entity has consented in writing, executed, acknowledged and filed in accordance with s 103`

-- "If the name of the foreign corporation conflicts with the name of a corporation, partnership, ... or a name
-- reserved or registered as that of a foreign corporation ..., the foreign corporation may qualify to do business if
-- it adopts an assumed name which shall be used when doing business in this State as long as the assumed name is
-- authorized for use by this section."
-- src:1836 | If the name of the foreign corporation conflicts with the name of a corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust organized under the laws of this State, or a name reserved for a corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust to be organized under the laws of this State, or a name reserved or registered as that of a foreign corporation, partnership, limited partnership, limited liability company or statutory trust under the laws of this State, the foreign corporation may qualify to do business if it adopts an assumed name which shall be used when doing business in this State as long as the assumed name is authorized for use by this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 371(c) (src:1836)
GIVEN `the name of the foreign corporation conflicts with another name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporation adopts an assumed name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assumed name is authorized for use by s 371(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 371(c) the foreign corporation may qualify to do business under an assumed name` `the name of the foreign corporation conflicts with another name` `the foreign corporation adopts an assumed name` `the assumed name is authorized for use by s 371(c)` MEANS
        `the name of the foreign corporation conflicts with another name`
    AND `the foreign corporation adopts an assumed name`
    AND `the assumed name is authorized for use by s 371(c)`

§§ `s 372 Additional requirements in case of change of name, change of business purpose or merger or consolidation`

-- (a): "within 30 days after the time said change becomes effective": the 30th day is inside (fork F1).
-- src:1840 | Every foreign corporation admitted to do business in this State which shall change its corporate name, or enlarge, limit or otherwise change the business which it proposes to do in this State, shall, within 30 days after the time said change becomes effective, file with the Secretary of State a certificate, which shall set forth:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a) (src:1840)
GIVEN `the date the change becomes effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 372(a) the last day for the foreign corporation to file the certificate of change` `the date the change becomes effective` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` `the date the change becomes effective`

-- src:1841 | (1) The name of the foreign corporation as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State of this State;
-- src:1842 | (2) The jurisdiction of its incorporation;
-- src:1843 | (3) The date it was authorized to do business in this State;
-- src:1844 | (4) If the name of the foreign corporation has been changed, a statement of the name relinquished, a statement of the new name and a statement that the change of name has been effected under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation and the date the change was effected;
-- src:1845 | (5) If the business it proposes to do in this State is to be enlarged, limited or otherwise changed, a statement reflecting such change and a statement that it is authorized to do in the jurisdiction of its incorporation the business which it proposes to do in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a) (src:1841-1845)
DECLARE `s 372(a) Certificate of change` HAS
    `the foreign corporation changed its corporate name`                                                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign corporation enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets forth the name of the foreign corporation as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets forth the jurisdiction of its incorporation`                                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate sets forth the date it was authorized to do business in this State`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states the name relinquished`                                                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states the new name`                                                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states that the change of name has been effected under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation and the date it was effected` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate contains a statement reflecting the change in the business`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the certificate states that the foreign corporation is authorized to do in the jurisdiction of its incorporation the business it proposes to do in this State` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1841 | (1) The name of the foreign corporation as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State of this State;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a)(1) (src:1841)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 372(a) Certificate of change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(a)(1) the certificate sets forth the name as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State` certificate MEANS
    certificate's `the certificate sets forth the name of the foreign corporation as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State`

-- src:1842 | (2) The jurisdiction of its incorporation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a)(2) (src:1842)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 372(a) Certificate of change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(a)(2) the certificate sets forth the jurisdiction of its incorporation` certificate MEANS
    certificate's `the certificate sets forth the jurisdiction of its incorporation`

-- src:1843 | (3) The date it was authorized to do business in this State;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a) (src:1843)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 372(a) Certificate of change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(a)(3) the certificate sets forth the date it was authorized to do business in this State` certificate MEANS
    certificate's `the certificate sets forth the date it was authorized to do business in this State`

-- src:1844 | (4) If the name of the foreign corporation has been changed, a statement of the name relinquished, a statement of the new name and a statement that the change of name has been effected under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation and the date the change was effected;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a)(4) (src:1844)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 372(a) Certificate of change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(a)(4) the certificate states the name relinquished, the new name and that the change was effected under the home law` certificate MEANS
        (NOT certificate's `the foreign corporation changed its corporate name`)
    OR  (    certificate's `the certificate states the name relinquished`
         AND certificate's `the certificate states the new name`
         AND certificate's `the certificate states that the change of name has been effected under the laws of the jurisdiction of its incorporation and the date it was effected`)

-- src:1845 | (5) If the business it proposes to do in this State is to be enlarged, limited or otherwise changed, a statement reflecting such change and a statement that it is authorized to do in the jurisdiction of its incorporation the business which it proposes to do in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a)(5) (src:1845)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 372(a) Certificate of change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(a)(5) the certificate reflects the change in the business and states that it is authorized at home` certificate MEANS
        (NOT certificate's `the foreign corporation enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State`)
    OR  (    certificate's `the certificate contains a statement reflecting the change in the business`
         AND certificate's `the certificate states that the foreign corporation is authorized to do in the jurisdiction of its incorporation the business it proposes to do in this State`)

-- src:1840 | (a) Every foreign corporation admitted to do business in this State which shall change its corporate name, or enlarge, limit or otherwise change the business which it proposes to do in this State, shall, within 30 days after the time said change becomes effective, file with the Secretary of State a certificate, which shall set forth:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(a) (src:1840)
GIVEN certificate IS A `s 372(a) Certificate of change`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(a) the certificate of change sets forth what the subsection requires` certificate MEANS
        `s 372(a)(1) the certificate sets forth the name as it appears on the records of the Secretary of State` certificate
    AND `s 372(a)(2) the certificate sets forth the jurisdiction of its incorporation` certificate
    AND `s 372(a)(3) the certificate sets forth the date it was authorized to do business in this State` certificate
    AND `s 372(a)(4) the certificate states the name relinquished, the new name and that the change was effected under the home law` certificate
    AND `s 372(a)(5) the certificate reflects the change in the business and states that it is authorized at home` certificate

-- (b): a survivor of a merger permitted by the laws of its home state or country files within 30 days after the merger
-- becomes effective a certificate issued by the proper officer of that state or country attesting to the event; if
-- the merger also changed the name or the business it also complies with (a).
-- src:1846 | (b) Whenever a foreign corporation authorized to transact business in this State shall be the survivor of a merger permitted by the laws of the state or country in which it is incorporated, it shall, within 30 days after the merger becomes effective, file a certificate, issued by the proper officer of the state or country of its incorporation, attesting to the occurrence of such event. If the merger has changed the corporate name of such foreign corporation or has enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State, it shall also comply with subsection (a) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(b) (src:1846)
GIVEN `the date the merger becomes effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 372(b) the last day for the surviving foreign corporation to file the certificate attesting to the merger` `the date the merger becomes effective` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 30) `after` `the date the merger becomes effective`

-- src:1846 | (b) Whenever a foreign corporation authorized to transact business in this State shall be the survivor of a merger permitted by the laws of the state or country in which it is incorporated, it shall, within 30 days after the merger becomes effective, file a certificate, issued by the proper officer of the state or country of its incorporation, attesting to the occurrence of such event. If the merger has changed the corporate name of such foreign corporation or has enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State, it shall also comply with subsection (a) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(b) (src:1846)
GIVEN `the certificate was issued by the proper officer of the state or country of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate attests to the occurrence of the merger` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(b) the certificate attesting to the merger is as the subsection requires` `the certificate was issued by the proper officer of the state or country of incorporation` `the certificate attests to the occurrence of the merger` MEANS
    `the certificate was issued by the proper officer of the state or country of incorporation` AND `the certificate attests to the occurrence of the merger`

-- src:1846 | (b) Whenever a foreign corporation authorized to transact business in this State shall be the survivor of a merger permitted by the laws of the state or country in which it is incorporated, it shall, within 30 days after the merger becomes effective, file a certificate, issued by the proper officer of the state or country of its incorporation, attesting to the occurrence of such event. If the merger has changed the corporate name of such foreign corporation or has enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State, it shall also comply with subsection (a) of this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(b) (src:1846)
GIVEN `the merger has changed the corporate name of the foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the merger has enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(b) the surviving foreign corporation must also comply with subsection (a)` `the merger has changed the corporate name of the foreign corporation` `the merger has enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State` MEANS
        `the merger has changed the corporate name of the foreign corporation`
    OR  `the merger has enlarged, limited or otherwise changed the business it proposes to do in this State`

-- src:1847 | (c) Whenever a foreign corporation authorized to transact business in this State ceases to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation, it shall comply with § 381 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(c) (src:1847)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation ceases to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 372(c) the foreign corporation must comply with s 381` `the foreign corporation ceases to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation` MEANS
    `the foreign corporation ceases to exist because of a statutory merger or consolidation`

-- (d): $50 for filing and indexing each certificate required by (a) or (b), and on a change of name a further $50 for
-- a certificate to be issued as evidence of filing the change of name (fork F25: payable whenever the name changed).
-- src:1848 | (d) The Secretary of State shall be paid, for the use of the State, $50 for filing and indexing each certificate required by subsection (a) or (b) of this section, and in the event of a change of name an additional $50 shall be paid for a certificate to be issued as evidence of filing the change of name.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 372(d) (src:1848)
GIVEN `the number of certificates filed under subsection (a) or (b)` IS A NUMBER
      `the foreign corporation changed its corporate name` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 372(d) the amount to be paid to the Secretary of State` `the number of certificates filed under subsection (a) or (b)` `the foreign corporation changed its corporate name` MEANS
    (50 TIMES `the number of certificates filed under subsection (a) or (b)`) PLUS (IF `the foreign corporation changed its corporate name` THEN 50 ELSE 0)

§§ `s 373 Exceptions to requirements`

-- src:1853 | (1) If it is in the mail order or a similar business, merely receiving orders by mail or otherwise in pursuance of letters, circulars, catalogs or other forms of advertising, or solicitation, accepting the orders outside this State, and filling them with goods shipped into this State;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(1) (src:1853)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation is in the mail order or a similar business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it merely receives orders by mail or otherwise in pursuance of letters, circulars, catalogs or other forms of advertising or solicitation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it accepts the orders outside this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it fills them with goods shipped into this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(1) the foreign corporation is excused as a mail order or similar business` `the foreign corporation is in the mail order or a similar business` `it merely receives orders by mail or otherwise in pursuance of letters, circulars, catalogs or other forms of advertising or solicitation` `it accepts the orders outside this State` `it fills them with goods shipped into this State` MEANS
        `the foreign corporation is in the mail order or a similar business`
    AND `it merely receives orders by mail or otherwise in pursuance of letters, circulars, catalogs or other forms of advertising or solicitation`
    AND `it accepts the orders outside this State`
    AND `it fills them with goods shipped into this State`

-- (2): samples kept in this State: a corporation that keeps none satisfies the condition; one that keeps some must keep
-- them for display or advertising purposes only.
-- src:1854 | (2) If it employs salespersons, either resident or traveling, to solicit orders in this State, either by display of samples or otherwise (whether or not maintaining sales offices in this State), all orders being subject to approval at the offices of the corporation without this State, and all goods applicable to the orders being shipped in pursuance thereof from without this State to the vendee or to the seller or such seller’s agent for delivery to the vendee, and if any samples kept within this State are for display or advertising purposes only, and no sales, repairs or replacements are made from stock on hand in this State;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(2) (src:1854)
GIVEN `it employs salespersons, either resident or traveling, to solicit orders in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all orders are subject to approval at the offices of the corporation without this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all goods applicable to the orders are shipped from without this State to the vendee or to the seller or such seller's agent for delivery to the vendee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it keeps samples within this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any samples kept within this State are for display or advertising purposes only` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no sales, repairs or replacements are made from stock on hand in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(2) the foreign corporation is excused as one soliciting orders through salespersons` `it employs salespersons, either resident or traveling, to solicit orders in this State` `all orders are subject to approval at the offices of the corporation without this State` `all goods applicable to the orders are shipped from without this State to the vendee or to the seller or such seller's agent for delivery to the vendee` `it keeps samples within this State` `any samples kept within this State are for display or advertising purposes only` `no sales, repairs or replacements are made from stock on hand in this State` MEANS
        `it employs salespersons, either resident or traveling, to solicit orders in this State`
    AND `all orders are subject to approval at the offices of the corporation without this State`
    AND `all goods applicable to the orders are shipped from without this State to the vendee or to the seller or such seller's agent for delivery to the vendee`
    AND ((NOT `it keeps samples within this State`) OR `any samples kept within this State are for display or advertising purposes only`)
    AND `no sales, repairs or replacements are made from stock on hand in this State`

-- src:1855 | (3) If it sells, by contract consummated outside this State, and agrees, by the contract, to deliver into this State, machinery, plants or equipment, the construction, erection or installation of which within this State requires the supervision of technical engineers or skilled employees performing services not generally available, and as a part of the contract of sale agrees to furnish such services, and such services only, to the vendee at the time of construction, erection or installation;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(3) (src:1855)
GIVEN `it sells by contract consummated outside this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it agrees by the contract to deliver into this State machinery, plants or equipment the construction, erection or installation of which requires the supervision of technical engineers or skilled employees performing services not generally available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `as a part of the contract of sale it agrees to furnish such services, and such services only, to the vendee at the time of construction, erection or installation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(3) the foreign corporation is excused as a seller of machinery, plants or equipment` `it sells by contract consummated outside this State` `it agrees by the contract to deliver into this State machinery, plants or equipment the construction, erection or installation of which requires the supervision of technical engineers or skilled employees performing services not generally available` `as a part of the contract of sale it agrees to furnish such services, and such services only, to the vendee at the time of construction, erection or installation` MEANS
        `it sells by contract consummated outside this State`
    AND `it agrees by the contract to deliver into this State machinery, plants or equipment the construction, erection or installation of which requires the supervision of technical engineers or skilled employees performing services not generally available`
    AND `as a part of the contract of sale it agrees to furnish such services, and such services only, to the vendee at the time of construction, erection or installation`

-- src:1856 | (4) If its business operations within this State, although not falling within the terms of paragraphs (a)(1), (2) and (3) of this section or any of them, are nevertheless wholly interstate in character;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(4) (src:1856)
GIVEN `its business operations within this State are wholly interstate in character` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(4) the foreign corporation is excused because its operations are wholly interstate` `its business operations within this State are wholly interstate in character` MEANS
    `its business operations within this State are wholly interstate in character`

-- src:1857 | (5) If it is an insurance company doing business in this State;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(5) (src:1857)
GIVEN `it is an insurance company doing business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(5) the foreign corporation is excused as an insurance company` `it is an insurance company doing business in this State` MEANS
    `it is an insurance company doing business in this State`

-- src:1858 | (6) If it creates, as borrower or lender, or acquires, evidences of debt, mortgages or liens on real or personal property;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(6) (src:1858)
GIVEN `it creates, as borrower or lender, or acquires, evidences of debt, mortgages or liens on real or personal property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(6) the foreign corporation is excused because it creates or acquires evidences of debt, mortgages or liens` `it creates, as borrower or lender, or acquires, evidences of debt, mortgages or liens on real or personal property` MEANS
    `it creates, as borrower or lender, or acquires, evidences of debt, mortgages or liens on real or personal property`

-- src:1859 | (7) If it secures or collects debts or enforces any rights in property securing the same.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a)(7) (src:1859)
GIVEN `it secures or collects debts or enforces any rights in property securing the same` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a)(7) the foreign corporation is excused because it secures or collects debts or enforces rights in property securing them` `it secures or collects debts or enforces any rights in property securing the same` MEANS
    `it secures or collects debts or enforces any rights in property securing the same`

-- "under any of the following conditions": the seven conditions are alternatives (fork F26).
-- src:1852 | (a) No foreign corporation shall be required to comply with §§ 371 and 372 of this title, under any of the following conditions:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(a) (src:1852)
GIVEN `the mail order condition in s 373(a)(1) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the salespersons condition in s 373(a)(2) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the machinery condition in s 373(a)(3) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the interstate condition in s 373(a)(4) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the insurance company condition in s 373(a)(5) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt condition in s 373(a)(6) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the collection condition in s 373(a)(7) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(a) the foreign corporation is not required to comply with ss 371 and 372` `the mail order condition in s 373(a)(1) is met` `the salespersons condition in s 373(a)(2) is met` `the machinery condition in s 373(a)(3) is met` `the interstate condition in s 373(a)(4) is met` `the insurance company condition in s 373(a)(5) is met` `the debt condition in s 373(a)(6) is met` `the collection condition in s 373(a)(7) is met` MEANS
        `the mail order condition in s 373(a)(1) is met`
    OR  `the salespersons condition in s 373(a)(2) is met`
    OR  `the machinery condition in s 373(a)(3) is met`
    OR  `the interstate condition in s 373(a)(4) is met`
    OR  `the insurance company condition in s 373(a)(5) is met`
    OR  `the debt condition in s 373(a)(6) is met`
    OR  `the collection condition in s 373(a)(7) is met`

-- (b): "This section shall have no application to the question of whether any foreign corporation is subject to
-- service of process and suit in this State under s 382 of this title or any other law of this State."
-- src:1860 | (b) This section shall have no application to the question of whether any foreign corporation is subject to service of process and suit in this State under § 382 of this title or any other law of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 373(b) (src:1860)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation is not required to comply with ss 371 and 372 under s 373(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 373(b) the exception settles whether the foreign corporation is subject to service of process and suit in this State` `the foreign corporation is not required to comply with ss 371 and 372 under s 373(a)` MEANS
    FALSE

§§ `s 374 Annual report`

-- "Annually on or before June 30, a foreign corporation doing business in this State shall file a report with the
-- Secretary of State." The last day is June 30 itself (fork F29).
-- src:1864 | Annually on or before June 30, a foreign corporation doing business in this State shall file a report with the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
GIVEN `the year of the report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 374 the last day to file the annual report for the year` `the year of the report` MEANS
    YMD `the year of the report` 6 30

-- src:1864 | Annually on or before June 30, a foreign corporation doing business in this State shall file a report with the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation is doing business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374 the foreign corporation must file an annual report with the Secretary of State` `the foreign corporation is doing business in this State` MEANS
    `the foreign corporation is doing business in this State`

-- src:1864 | Annually on or before June 30, a foreign corporation doing business in this State shall file a report with the Secretary of State. The report shall be made on a form designated by the Secretary of State and shall be signed by the corporation's president, secretary, treasurer or other proper officer duly authorized so to act, or by any of its directors, or if filing an initial report by any incorporator in the event its board of directors shall not have been elected. The fact that an individual’s name is signed on a certification attached to a corporate report shall be prima facie evidence that such individual is authorized to certify the report on behalf of the corporation; however the official title or position of the individual signing the corporate report shall be designated. The report shall contain the following information:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
GIVEN `the year of the report` IS A NUMBER
      `the date the report was filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374 the annual report was filed in time` `the year of the report` `the date the report was filed` MEANS
    `the date the report was filed` AT MOST (`s 374 the last day to file the annual report for the year` `the year of the report`)

-- Who signs: "the corporation's president, secretary, treasurer or other proper officer duly authorized so to act, or
-- by any of its directors, or if filing an initial report by any incorporator in the event its board of directors
-- shall not have been elected".
-- src:1864 | The report shall be made on a form designated by the Secretary of State and shall be signed by the corporation's president, secretary, treasurer or other proper officer duly authorized so to act, or by any of its directors, or if filing an initial report by any incorporator in the event its board of directors shall not have been elected. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
DECLARE `s 374 Person who signs the annual report` IS ONE OF
    `the corporation's president under s 374`
    `the corporation's secretary under s 374`
    `the corporation's treasurer under s 374`
    `another proper officer duly authorized so to act under s 374`
    `one of the corporation's directors under s 374`
    `an incorporator under s 374`
    `a person who is none of these under s 374`

-- src:1864 | The report shall be made on a form designated by the Secretary of State and shall be signed by the corporation's president, secretary, treasurer or other proper officer duly authorized so to act, or by any of its directors, or if filing an initial report by any incorporator in the event its board of directors shall not have been elected. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
GIVEN signer IS A `s 374 Person who signs the annual report`
      `the report is an initial report` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board of directors has been elected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374 the person may sign the annual report` signer `the report is an initial report` `the board of directors has been elected` MEANS
    CONSIDER signer
    WHEN `an incorporator under s 374` THEN `the report is an initial report` AND (NOT `the board of directors has been elected`)
    WHEN `a person who is none of these under s 374` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:1864 | The report shall be made on a form designated by the Secretary of State and shall be signed by the corporation's president, secretary, treasurer or other proper officer duly authorized so to act, or by any of its directors, or if filing an initial report by any incorporator in the event its board of directors shall not have been elected. The fact that an individual’s name is signed on a certification attached to a corporate report shall be prima facie evidence that such individual is authorized to certify the report on behalf of the corporation; however the official title or position of the individual signing the corporate report shall be designated. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
GIVEN `the report is made on a form designated by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person who signed the report is one the section allows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the official title or position of the individual signing the report is designated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374 the report is made and signed as the section requires` `the report is made on a form designated by the Secretary of State` `the person who signed the report is one the section allows` `the official title or position of the individual signing the report is designated` MEANS
        `the report is made on a form designated by the Secretary of State`
    AND `the person who signed the report is one the section allows`
    AND `the official title or position of the individual signing the report is designated`

-- "The fact that an individual's name is signed on a certification attached to a corporate report shall be prima
-- facie evidence that such individual is authorized to certify the report on behalf of the corporation".
-- src:1864 | The fact that an individual’s name is signed on a certification attached to a corporate report shall be prima facie evidence that such individual is authorized to certify the report on behalf of the corporation; …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1864)
GIVEN `an individual's name is signed on a certification attached to the corporate report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374 the signature is prima facie evidence that the individual is authorized to certify the report` `an individual's name is signed on a certification attached to the corporate report` MEANS
    `an individual's name is signed on a certification attached to the corporate report`

-- src:1865 | (1) The location of its registered office in this State, which shall include the street, number, city and postal code;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374(1) (src:1865)
GIVEN `the report gives the location of the registered office in this State, including the street, number, city and postal code` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374(1) the report contains the location of the registered office` `the report gives the location of the registered office in this State, including the street, number, city and postal code` MEANS
    `the report gives the location of the registered office in this State, including the street, number, city and postal code`

-- src:1866 | (2) The name of the agent upon whom service of process against the corporation may be served;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374(2) (src:1866)
GIVEN `the report gives the name of the agent upon whom service of process against the corporation may be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374(2) the report contains the name of the agent for service of process` `the report gives the name of the agent upon whom service of process against the corporation may be served` MEANS
    `the report gives the name of the agent upon whom service of process against the corporation may be served`

-- src:1867 | (3) The location of the principal place of business of the corporation, which shall include the street, number, city, state or foreign country; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374(3) (src:1867)
GIVEN `the report gives the location of the principal place of business, including the street, number, city, state or foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374(3) the report contains the location of the principal place of business` `the report gives the location of the principal place of business, including the street, number, city, state or foreign country` MEANS
    `the report gives the location of the principal place of business, including the street, number, city, state or foreign country`

-- src:1868 | (4) The names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date of the report and the name and address of the officer who signs the report.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374(4) (src:1868)
GIVEN `the report gives the names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report gives the name and address of the officer who signs it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374(4) the report contains the names and addresses of the directors and of the signing officer` `the report gives the names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date` `the report gives the name and address of the officer who signs it` MEANS
    `the report gives the names and addresses of all the directors as of the filing date` AND `the report gives the name and address of the officer who signs it`

-- src:1869 | If any officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file an annual report with the Secretary of State shall knowingly make any false statement in the report, such officer or director shall be guilty of perjury.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 374 (src:1869)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file an annual report with the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knowingly made a false statement in the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 374 the officer or director is guilty of perjury` `the person is an officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file an annual report with the Secretary of State` `the person knowingly made a false statement in the report` MEANS
    `the person is an officer or director of a foreign corporation required to file an annual report with the Secretary of State` AND `the person knowingly made a false statement in the report`

§§ `s 375 Failure to file report`

-- src:1873 | Upon the failure, neglect or refusal of any foreign corporation to file an annual report as required by § 374 of this title, the Secretary of State may, in the Secretary of State’s discretion, investigate the reasons therefor …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 375 (src:1873)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation failed, neglected or refused to file an annual report as required by s 374` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 375 the Secretary of State may investigate the reasons for the failure` `the foreign corporation failed, neglected or refused to file an annual report as required by s 374` MEANS
    `the foreign corporation failed, neglected or refused to file an annual report as required by s 374`

-- "shall terminate the right of the foreign corporation to do business within this State upon failure of the
-- corporation to file an annual report within any 2-year period": no report within the 2 years after the last one
-- (fork F27); where none was ever filed the text does not say from when the 2 years run (NOTHING).
-- src:1873 | and shall terminate the right of the foreign corporation to do business within this State upon failure of the corporation to file an annual report within any 2-year period.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 375 (src:1873)
GIVEN `the date the last annual report was filed, if one was ever filed` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 375 the Secretary of State must terminate the right of the foreign corporation to do business within this State` `the date the last annual report was filed, if one was ever filed` `the date asked about` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the last annual report was filed, if one was ever filed`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the date asked about` GREATER THAN (`the date` (`period in years` 2) `after` last))

§§ `s 376 Service of process upon qualified foreign corporations`

-- (a): process, orders, rules and notices may be served on the registered agent designated in accordance with s 371,
-- or, if there is no such agent, on any officer, director or other agent of the corporation then in this State.
-- src:1877 | (a) All process issued out of any court of this State, all orders made by any court of this State, all rules and notices of any kind required to be served on any foreign corporation which has qualified to do business in this State may be served on the registered agent of the corporation designated in accordance with § 371 of this title, or, if there be no such agent, then on any officer, director or other agent of the corporation then in this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(a) (src:1877)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person served is the registered agent designated in accordance with s 371` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has such a registered agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person served is an officer, director or other agent of the corporation then in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(a) the process, order, rule or notice may be served on the person` `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State` `the person served is the registered agent designated in accordance with s 371` `the corporation has such a registered agent` `the person served is an officer, director or other agent of the corporation then in this State` MEANS
        `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State`
    AND (    `the person served is the registered agent designated in accordance with s 371`
         OR  ((NOT `the corporation has such a registered agent`) AND `the person served is an officer, director or other agent of the corporation then in this State`))

-- (b): the same as s 321(b), with the letter going to the principal place of business "as it appears on the last
-- annual report filed pursuant to s 374" or, if no such address appears, the last registered office.
-- src:1878 | In case the officer whose duty it is to serve legal process cannot by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided for by subsection (a) of this section, it shall be lawful to serve the process against the corporation upon the Secretary of State, and such service shall be as effectual for all intents and purposes as if made in any of the ways provided for in subsection (a) of this section. Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 376(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) service on the Secretary of State is as effectual as service under subsection (a)` `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 376(a)` `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission` `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made` MEANS
        `the process server could not by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided in s 376(a)`
    AND (    (NOT `the process was served on the Secretary of State by electronic transmission`)
          OR `the Secretary of State has prescribed service by electronic transmission in the way it was made`)

-- src:1878 | the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the last annual report filed pursuant to § 374 of this title or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN `an address for the principal place of business appears on the last annual report filed under s 374` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the letter was directed to the last registered office of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) the letter is addressed as the subsection requires` `an address for the principal place of business appears on the last annual report filed under s 374` `the letter was directed to that principal place of business` `the letter was directed to the last registered office of the corporation` MEANS
    IF `an address for the principal place of business appears on the last annual report filed under s 374`
    THEN `the letter was directed to that principal place of business`
    ELSE `the letter was directed to the last registered office of the corporation`

-- The Secretary of State's letter, the plaintiff's steps, the fee, the record and its retention are those of s 321(b).
-- src:1878 | (b) In case the officer whose duty it is to serve legal process cannot by due diligence serve the process in any manner provided for by subsection (a) of this section, it shall be lawful to serve the process against the corporation upon the Secretary of State, and such service shall be as effectual for all intents and purposes as if made in any of the ways provided for in subsection (a) of this section. Process may be served upon the Secretary of State under this subsection by means of electronic transmission but only as prescribed by the Secretary of State. The Secretary of State is authorized to issue such rules and regulations with respect to such service as the Secretary of State deems necessary or appropriate. In the event that service is effected through the Secretary of State in accordance with this subsection, the Secretary of State shall forthwith notify the corporation by letter, directed to the corporation at its principal place of business as it appears on the last annual report filed pursuant to § 374 of this title or, if no such address appears, at its last registered office. Such letter shall be sent by a mail or courier service that includes a record of mailing or deposit with the courier and a record of delivery evidenced by the signature of the recipient. Such letter shall enclose a copy of the process and any other papers served upon the Secretary of State pursuant to this subsection. It shall be the duty of the plaintiff in the event of such service to serve process and any other papers in duplicate, to notify the Secretary of State that service is being effected pursuant to this subsection, and to pay the Secretary of State a fee as prescribed under § 391(a)(29) of this title for the use of the State, which sum shall be taxed as a part of the costs in the proceeding if the plaintiff shall prevail therein. The Secretary of State shall maintain an alphabetical record of any such service setting forth the name of the plaintiff and the defendant, the title, docket number and nature of the proceeding in which process has been served upon the Secretary of State, the fact that service has been effected pursuant to this subsection, the return date thereof, and the day and hour when the service was made. The Secretary of State shall not be required to retain such information for a period longer than 5 years from receipt of such service.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN `the letter` IS A `s 321(b) Letter from the Secretary of State`
      `the letter was addressed as s 376(b) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) the Secretary of State's letter meets the subsection` `the letter` `the letter was addressed as s 376(b) requires` MEANS
    `s 321(b) the Secretary of State's letter meets the section` `the letter` `the letter was addressed as s 376(b) requires`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN steps IS A `s 321(b) Plaintiff's steps`
      `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)` IS A NUMBER  -- out of range: section 391(a)(29) (piece dg11)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` steps `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)` MEANS
    `s 321(b) the plaintiff has done what the subsection requires` steps `the fee prescribed under s 391(a)(29)`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) the fee is taxed as part of the costs` `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding` MEANS
    `s 321(b) the fee is taxed as part of the costs` `the plaintiff prevails in the proceeding`

@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN record IS A `s 321(b) Record of service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) the record of service lists what the subsection requires` record MEANS
    `s 321(b) the record of service lists what the subsection requires` record

@ref 8 Del. C. § 376(b) (src:1878)
GIVEN `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` IS A DATE
      `the date the record is asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 376(b) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date the record is asked about` MEANS
    `s 321(b) the Secretary of State must still retain the record of service` `the date the Secretary of State received the service of process` `the date the record is asked about`

§§ `s 377 Change of registered agent; reinstatement of qualification to do business`

-- (a): the foreign corporation, qualified to do business in this State, changes its registered agent by filing a
-- certificate with the Secretary of State, acknowledged in accordance with s 103, setting forth the name and address of
-- the new agent and a revocation of all previous appointments; "Such registered agent shall comply with s 371(b)(2)(i)".
-- src:1882 | (a) Any foreign corporation, which has qualified to do business in this State, may change its registered agent and substitute another registered agent by filing a certificate with the Secretary of State, acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, setting forth:
-- src:1883 | (1) The name and address of its registered agent designated in this State upon whom process directed to said corporation may be served; and
-- src:1884 | (2) A revocation of all previous appointments of agent for such purposes.
-- src:1885 | Such registered agent shall comply with § 371(b)(2)(i) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(a) (src:1882-1885)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate was filed with the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate was acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 103 (piece dg1)
      `the certificate sets forth the name and address of the registered agent designated in this State upon whom process may be served` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth a revocation of all previous appointments of agent for such purposes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the new registered agent is one that s 371(b)(2)(i) allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 377(a) the foreign corporation has changed its registered agent` `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State` `the certificate was filed with the Secretary of State` `the certificate was acknowledged in accordance with s 103` `the certificate sets forth the name and address of the registered agent designated in this State upon whom process may be served` `the certificate sets forth a revocation of all previous appointments of agent for such purposes` `the new registered agent is one that s 371(b)(2)(i) allows` MEANS
        `the foreign corporation has qualified to do business in this State`
    AND `the certificate was filed with the Secretary of State`
    AND `the certificate was acknowledged in accordance with s 103`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the name and address of the registered agent designated in this State upon whom process may be served`
    AND `the certificate sets forth a revocation of all previous appointments of agent for such purposes`
    AND `the new registered agent is one that s 371(b)(2)(i) allows`

-- src:1886 | (b) Any individual or entity designated by a foreign corporation as its registered agent for service of process may resign in the same manner as provided in § 136(a) of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(b) (src:1886)
GIVEN `the individual or entity designated as registered agent resigns in the same manner as s 136(a) provides` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: section 136(a) (piece dg2)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 377(b) the registered agent has resigned` `the individual or entity designated as registered agent resigns in the same manner as s 136(a) provides` MEANS
    `the individual or entity designated as registered agent resigns in the same manner as s 136(a) provides`

-- (c): "within 10 days after the death, removal or resignation of its agent": the 10th day is inside (fork F1).
-- src:1887 | (c) If any agent designated and certified as required by § 371 of this title shall die or remove from this State, or resign, then the foreign corporation for which the agent had been so designated and certified shall, within 10 days after the death, removal or resignation of its agent, substitute, designate and certify to the Secretary of State, the name of another registered agent for the purposes of this subchapter, and all process, orders, rules and notices mentioned in § 376 of this title may be served on or given to the substituted agent with like effect as is prescribed in that section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(c) (src:1887)
GIVEN `the date the agent died, removed from this State or resigned` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 377(c) the last day for the foreign corporation to designate and certify another registered agent` `the date the agent died, removed from this State or resigned` MEANS
    `the date` (`period in days` 10) `after` `the date the agent died, removed from this State or resigned`

-- src:1887 | (c) If any agent designated and certified as required by § 371 of this title shall die or remove from this State, or resign, then the foreign corporation for which the agent had been so designated and certified shall, within 10 days after the death, removal or resignation of its agent, substitute, designate and certify to the Secretary of State, the name of another registered agent for the purposes of this subchapter, and all process, orders, rules and notices mentioned in § 376 of this title may be served on or given to the substituted agent with like effect as is prescribed in that section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(c) (src:1887)
GIVEN `the date the agent died, removed from this State or resigned` IS A DATE
      `the date the foreign corporation designated and certified to the Secretary of State the name of another registered agent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 377(c) the foreign corporation designated and certified another registered agent in time` `the date the agent died, removed from this State or resigned` `the date the foreign corporation designated and certified to the Secretary of State the name of another registered agent` MEANS
    `the date the foreign corporation designated and certified to the Secretary of State the name of another registered agent` AT MOST (`s 377(c) the last day for the foreign corporation to designate and certify another registered agent` `the date the agent died, removed from this State or resigned`)

-- "all process, orders, rules and notices mentioned in s 376 of this title may be served on or given to the substituted
-- agent with like effect as is prescribed in that section."
-- src:1887 | and all process, orders, rules and notices mentioned in § 376 of this title may be served on or given to the substituted agent with like effect as is prescribed in that section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(c) (src:1887)
GIVEN `another registered agent has been substituted, designated and certified to the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 377(c) process, orders, rules and notices may be served on or given to the substituted agent with like effect` `another registered agent has been substituted, designated and certified to the Secretary of State` MEANS
    `another registered agent has been substituted, designated and certified to the Secretary of State`

-- (d): reinstatement after a forfeiture under s 132(f)(4) or s 136(b).
-- src:1888 | (d) A foreign corporation whose qualification to do business in this State has been forfeited pursuant to § 132(f)(4) or § 136(b) of this title may be reinstated by filing a certificate of reinstatement with the Secretary of State, acknowledged in accordance with § 103 of this title, setting forth:
-- src:1889 | (1) The name of the foreign corporation;
-- src:1890 | (2) The effective date of the forfeiture; and
-- src:1891 | (3) The name and address of the foreign corporation’s registered agent required to be maintained by § 132 of this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(d) (src:1888-1891)
GIVEN `the qualification was forfeited pursuant to s 132(f)(4) or s 136(b)` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: sections 132 and 136 (piece dg2)
      `the certificate of reinstatement was filed with the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of reinstatement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the name of the foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the effective date of the forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets forth the name and address of the registered agent required to be maintained by s 132` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 377(d) the foreign corporation has filed a proper certificate of reinstatement` `the qualification was forfeited pursuant to s 132(f)(4) or s 136(b)` `the certificate of reinstatement was filed with the Secretary of State` `the certificate of reinstatement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103` `the certificate sets forth the name of the foreign corporation` `the certificate sets forth the effective date of the forfeiture` `the certificate sets forth the name and address of the registered agent required to be maintained by s 132` MEANS
        `the qualification was forfeited pursuant to s 132(f)(4) or s 136(b)`
    AND `the certificate of reinstatement was filed with the Secretary of State`
    AND `the certificate of reinstatement was acknowledged in accordance with s 103`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the name of the foreign corporation`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the effective date of the forfeiture`
    AND `the certificate sets forth the name and address of the registered agent required to be maintained by s 132`

-- src:1892 | (e) Upon the filing of a certificate of reinstatement in accordance with subsection (d) of this section, and the filing of all annual reports and the payment of all required fees that would have been required to be filed and paid during the time the foreign corporation’s qualification to do business in this State had been forfeited, the qualification of the foreign corporation to do business in this State shall be reinstated with the same force and effect as if it had not been forfeited pursuant to this title.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 377(e) (src:1892)
GIVEN `the foreign corporation has filed a proper certificate of reinstatement under s 377(d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the annual reports that would have been required to be filed during the forfeiture have been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the fees that would have been required to be paid during the forfeiture have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 377(e) the qualification of the foreign corporation is reinstated with the same force and effect as if it had not been forfeited` `the foreign corporation has filed a proper certificate of reinstatement under s 377(d)` `all the annual reports that would have been required to be filed during the forfeiture have been filed` `all the fees that would have been required to be paid during the forfeiture have been paid` MEANS
        `the foreign corporation has filed a proper certificate of reinstatement under s 377(d)`
    AND `all the annual reports that would have been required to be filed during the forfeiture have been filed`
    AND `all the fees that would have been required to be paid during the forfeiture have been paid`

§§ `s 378 Penalties for noncompliance`

-- src:1896 | Any foreign corporation doing business of any kind in this State without first having complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $200 nor more than $500 for each such offense. Any agent of any foreign corporation that shall do any business in this State for any foreign corporation before the foreign corporation has complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $100 nor more than $500 for each such offense.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 378 (src:1896)
DECLARE `s 378 Offender` IS ONE OF
    `a foreign corporation doing business in this State without having complied, under s 378`
    `an agent of a foreign corporation doing business for it before it has complied, under s 378`

-- src:1896 | Any foreign corporation doing business of any kind in this State without first having complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $200 nor more than $500 for each such offense. Any agent of any foreign corporation that shall do any business in this State for any foreign corporation before the foreign corporation has complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $100 nor more than $500 for each such offense.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 378 (src:1896)
DECLARE `s 378 Fine for each offense` HAS
    `the lowest fine for each offense under s 378`  IS A NUMBER
    `the highest fine for each offense under s 378` IS A NUMBER

-- A foreign corporation doing business of any kind in this State without first having complied with any section of the
-- subchapter applicable to it is fined not less than $200 nor more than $500 for each offense; its agent that does
-- business for it before it has complied, not less than $100 nor more than $500 for each offense.
-- src:1896 | Any foreign corporation doing business of any kind in this State without first having complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $200 nor more than $500 for each such offense. Any agent of any foreign corporation that shall do any business in this State for any foreign corporation before the foreign corporation has complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $100 nor more than $500 for each such offense.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 378 (src:1896)
GIVEN offender IS A `s 378 Offender`
GIVETH A `s 378 Fine for each offense`
`s 378 the fine for each offense` offender MEANS
    CONSIDER offender
    WHEN `a foreign corporation doing business in this State without having complied, under s 378` THEN `s 378 Fine for each offense` WITH `the lowest fine for each offense under s 378` IS 200
                                                                                                                                     , `the highest fine for each offense under s 378` IS 500
    WHEN `an agent of a foreign corporation doing business for it before it has complied, under s 378` THEN `s 378 Fine for each offense` WITH `the lowest fine for each offense under s 378` IS 100
                                                                                                                                                   , `the highest fine for each offense under s 378` IS 500

-- src:1896 | Any foreign corporation doing business of any kind in this State without first having complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $200 nor more than $500 for each such offense. Any agent of any foreign corporation that shall do any business in this State for any foreign corporation before the foreign corporation has complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $100 nor more than $500 for each such offense.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 378 (src:1896)
GIVEN offender IS A `s 378 Offender`
      `the fine imposed for the offense` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 378 the fine imposed for the offense is within the range` offender `the fine imposed for the offense` MEANS
        `the fine imposed for the offense` AT LEAST (`s 378 the fine for each offense` offender)'s `the lowest fine for each offense under s 378`
    AND `the fine imposed for the offense` AT MOST (`s 378 the fine for each offense` offender)'s `the highest fine for each offense under s 378`

-- src:1896 | Any foreign corporation doing business of any kind in this State without first having complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $200 nor more than $500 for each such offense. Any agent of any foreign corporation that shall do any business in this State for any foreign corporation before the foreign corporation has complied with any section of this subchapter applicable to it, shall be fined not less than $100 nor more than $500 for each such offense.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 378 (src:1896)
GIVEN `the person does business of any kind in this State for a foreign corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the foreign corporation has not first complied with a section of this subchapter applicable to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 378 the doing of business is an offense` `the person does business of any kind in this State for a foreign corporation` `the foreign corporation has not first complied with a section of this subchapter applicable to it` MEANS
    `the person does business of any kind in this State for a foreign corporation` AND `the foreign corporation has not first complied with a section of this subchapter applicable to it`

§§ `s 379 Banking powers denied`

-- src:1900 | (a) No foreign corporation shall, within the limits of this State, by any implication or construction, be deemed to possess the power of discounting bills, notes or other evidence of debt, of receiving deposits, of buying and selling bills of exchange, or of issuing bills, notes or other evidences of debt upon loan for circulation as money, anything in its charter or articles of incorporation to the contrary notwithstanding, except as otherwise provided in subchapter VII of Chapter 7 or in Chapter 14 of Title 5.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 379(a) (src:1900)
DECLARE `s 379(a) Banking power` IS ONE OF
    `discounting bills, notes or other evidence of debt, under s 379(a)`
    `receiving deposits, under s 379(a)`
    `buying and selling bills of exchange, under s 379(a)`
    `issuing bills, notes or other evidences of debt upon loan for circulation as money, under s 379(a)`
    `a power that s 379(a) does not list`

-- No foreign corporation shall within this State be deemed to possess such a power, by implication or construction,
-- notwithstanding its charter, except as otherwise provided in subchapter VII of Chapter 7 or in Chapter 14 of Title 5
-- (not among the inputs). Where Title 5 provides otherwise, or the power is not listed, the section does not answer
-- (fork F34).
-- src:1900 | (a) No foreign corporation shall, within the limits of this State, by any implication or construction, be deemed to possess the power of discounting bills, notes or other evidence of debt, of receiving deposits, of buying and selling bills of exchange, or of issuing bills, notes or other evidences of debt upon loan for circulation as money, anything in its charter or articles of incorporation to the contrary notwithstanding, except as otherwise provided in subchapter VII of Chapter 7 or in Chapter 14 of Title 5.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 379(a) (src:1900)
GIVEN power IS A `s 379(a) Banking power`
      `Title 5 otherwise provides, in subchapter VII of Chapter 7 or in Chapter 14` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 379(a) the foreign corporation is deemed within this State to possess the power by implication or construction` power `Title 5 otherwise provides, in subchapter VII of Chapter 7 or in Chapter 14` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `a power that s 379(a) does not list` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE (IF `Title 5 otherwise provides, in subchapter VII of Chapter 7 or in Chapter 14` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE)

-- src:1901 | (b) All certificates issued by the Secretary of State under § 371 of this title shall expressly set forth the limitations and restrictions contained in this section.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 379(b) (src:1901)
GIVEN `the certificate issued by the Secretary of State under s 371 expressly sets forth the limitations and restrictions contained in s 379` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 379(b) the certificate meets the requirement to set forth the limitations and restrictions` `the certificate issued by the Secretary of State under s 371 expressly sets forth the limitations and restrictions contained in s 379` MEANS
    `the certificate issued by the Secretary of State under s 371 expressly sets forth the limitations and restrictions contained in s 379`

§§ `s 380 Foreign corporation as fiduciary in this State`

-- "A corporation organized and doing business under the laws of the District of Columbia or of any state of the United
-- States other than Delaware" -- not a territory or possession (fork F30).
-- src:1905 | A corporation organized and doing business under the laws of the District of Columbia or of any state of the United States other than Delaware, duly authorized by its certificate of incorporation or bylaws so to act, may be appointed by any last will and testament or other testamentary writing, probated within this State, or by a deed of trust, mortgage or other agreement, as executor, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary, and may act as such within this State, when and to the extent that the laws of the District of Columbia or of the state in which the foreign corporation is organized confer like powers upon corporations organized and doing business under the laws of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 380 (src:1905)
GIVEN `the corporation is organized and doing business under the laws of the District of Columbia or of a state of the United States other than Delaware` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is duly authorized by its certificate of incorporation or bylaws so to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is appointed by a last will and testament or other testamentary writing probated within this State, or by a deed of trust, mortgage or other agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the laws of the District of Columbia or of the state in which it is organized confer like powers upon corporations organized and doing business under the laws of this State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 380 the corporation may act within this State as executor, guardian, trustee or other fiduciary` `the corporation is organized and doing business under the laws of the District of Columbia or of a state of the United States other than Delaware` `it is duly authorized by its certificate of incorporation or bylaws so to act` `it is appointed by a last will and testament or other testamentary writing probated within this State, or by a deed of trust, mortgage or other agreement` `the laws of the District of Columbia or of the state in which it is organized confer like powers upon corporations organized and doing business under the laws of this State` MEANS
        `the corporation is organized and doing business under the laws of the District of Columbia or of a state of the United States other than Delaware`
    AND `it is duly authorized by its certificate of incorporation or bylaws so to act`
    AND `it is appointed by a last will and testament or other testamentary writing probated within this State, or by a deed of trust, mortgage or other agreement`
    AND `the laws of the District of Columbia or of the state in which it is organized confer like powers upon corporations organized and doing business under the laws of this State`
